642
00:27:22.210 --> 00:27:24.330
Does the office buy the chairs or the building?
到底是办公室买椅子，还是大楼买椅子？

643
00:27:25.170 --> 00:27:26.370
Are you asking me?
你是在问我吗？

644
00:27:27.010 --> 00:27:29.990
I think Christian is, has a little sass.
我觉得克里斯蒂安有点调皮。

645
00:27:30.330 --> 00:27:32.290
Christian, Jenna just looked at me like, and?
克里斯蒂安，珍娜刚才看着我，那眼神仿佛在说，那又怎样？

646
00:27:32.290 --> 00:27:33.370
What do you think, Angela?
安吉拉，你怎么看？

647
00:27:33.630 --> 00:27:34.770
I think, um.
我觉得，嗯。

648
00:27:34.970 --> 00:27:36.950
Why is Dwight worried about the chairs so much?
为什么德怀特这么担心椅子的问题？

649
00:27:36.950 --> 00:27:38.310
I think the building buys the chairs.
我觉得是大楼负责买椅子。

650
00:27:38.570 --> 00:27:39.650
That makes no sense.
这根本说不通。

651
00:27:41.010 --> 00:27:42.530
Well, then don't ask me.
那你就别问我了。

652
00:27:42.730 --> 00:27:46.230
Why did we have a whole episode where we argued over what to do with our surplus if
既然大楼无论如何都会给我们买椅子，

653
00:27:46.230 --> 00:27:48.130
the building would have just bought us chairs anyway?
那我们为什么还要花整整一集的时间争论盈余该怎么花？

654
00:27:48.130 --> 00:27:49.070
I don't know.
我不知道。

655
00:27:49.350 --> 00:27:55.990
I mean, I think very clearly the office has a budget to buy chairs for the office.
我的意思是，我觉得办公室显然有预算来购买办公椅。

656
00:27:55.990 --> 00:27:57.570
But, you know, there are other chairs.
但你知道，还有其他的椅子。

657
00:27:57.830 --> 00:28:00.230
There are the chairs of Caffeine Corner, perhaps.
也许有咖啡角的椅子。

658
00:28:00.230 --> 00:28:01.830
There are building chairs.
还有大楼的椅子。

659
00:28:02.050 --> 00:28:02.850
The lobby sofa.
大厅的沙发。

660
00:28:03.270 --> 00:28:03.870
Yes.
没错。

661
00:28:04.250 --> 00:28:05.150
There you go.
就是这样。

662
00:28:06.130 --> 00:28:07.290
Maybe it's both.
也许两者都有。

663
00:28:07.430 --> 00:28:08.370
Case of the chairs.
椅子疑案。

664
00:28:11.250 --> 00:28:14.310
Well, Andy is going to start showing Susan around.
安迪要开始带苏珊参观了。

665
00:28:14.310 --> 00:28:18.730
And right before they start their tour, she says goodbye to a few folks.
就在他们开始参观之前，她和几个人道了别。

666
00:28:19.450 --> 00:28:19.690
Yes.
是的。

667
00:28:19.830 --> 00:28:21.570
And she gets Ryan's name wrong.
她还把瑞安的名字叫错了。

668
00:28:21.570 --> 00:28:23.990
As she's saying goodbye, she calls him Brian.
她在道别时叫他布莱恩。

669
00:28:24.250 --> 00:28:26.290
And he is not pleased.
他很不高兴。

670
00:28:26.790 --> 00:28:28.570
This is something I struggle with.
这是我一直很头疼的问题。

671
00:28:28.910 --> 00:28:30.110
Anyone else out there?
还有其他人也这样吗？

672
00:28:30.290 --> 00:28:35.310
Like Ryan and Brian, Craig and Greg, Kristen, Christine, Tim and Tom.
就像瑞安和布莱恩、克雷格和格雷格、克里斯汀和克里斯汀、蒂姆和汤姆。

673
00:28:35.630 --> 00:28:37.150
I'm going to get it wrong, guys.
伙计们，我肯定会叫错的。

674
00:28:37.790 --> 00:28:38.950
Tamara, Tamara.
塔玛拉，塔玛拉。

675
00:28:39.310 --> 00:28:40.250
I'm going to get it wrong.
我肯定会叫错的。

676
00:28:40.350 --> 00:28:41.610
And I'm so sorry.
对此我深感抱歉。

677
00:28:41.610 --> 00:28:43.270
I don't mean anything by it.
我真的不是故意的。

678
00:28:43.730 --> 00:28:46.290
It's a hard thing sometimes to dial in.
有时候这确实很难拿捏。

679
00:28:46.390 --> 00:28:47.210
Wait, which one was it?
等等，到底是哪一个？

680
00:28:47.270 --> 00:28:47.930
Ryan or Brian?
瑞安还是布莱恩？

681
00:28:48.470 --> 00:28:52.230
And then, you know, I wonder if, like, behind your back, someone's like, bitch.
然后我就在想，会不会有人在背后骂我贱人。

682
00:28:52.230 --> 00:29:00.330
There are so many parents at my kid's school who were probably introduced to me in the beginning.
我孩子学校里有很多家长，可能刚开始时有人向我介绍过他们。

683
00:29:00.830 --> 00:29:03.590
But now we're, like, five grades deep.
但现在我们孩子都上到五年级了。

684
00:29:03.750 --> 00:29:04.330
It's too late.
太晚了。

685
00:29:04.410 --> 00:29:05.090
It's too late.
太晚了。

686
00:29:05.250 --> 00:29:07.170
You've got the name wrong, and it's too late.
名字叫错了，现在已经太晚了。

687
00:29:07.430 --> 00:29:10.010
There's a dad at our school who calls everyone friend.
我们学校有个爸爸管谁都叫朋友。

688
00:29:10.590 --> 00:29:11.570
Oh, he doesn't know anyone's name.
哦，他根本不知道任何人的名字。

689
00:29:11.570 --> 00:29:12.590
I don't think he knows anyone's name.
我觉得他谁的名字都不知道。

690
00:29:12.730 --> 00:29:12.910
No.
没错。

691
00:29:13.250 --> 00:29:14.330
But I can't do it.
但我做不到。

692
00:29:14.350 --> 00:29:15.550
I can't pull that off.
我没法那样做。

693
00:29:15.710 --> 00:29:15.910
Yeah.
是啊。

694
00:29:16.050 --> 00:29:17.750
My husband does a lot of, like, what's up, buddy?
我丈夫经常说，嘿，伙计，最近怎么样？

695
00:29:17.970 --> 00:29:18.850
And I'm like, you don't.
我就跟他说，你根本不认识人家。

696
00:29:18.890 --> 00:29:20.230
Men can do it better.
男人在这方面做得更好。

697
00:29:20.490 --> 00:29:20.890
Stop saying buddy.
别再叫人家伙计了。

698
00:29:20.890 --> 00:29:22.410
We all know you don't know their name.
我们都知道你根本不知道他们的名字。

699
00:29:22.530 --> 00:29:25.110
Men have dude, buddy, man.
男人有“哥们”、“伙计”、“兄弟”这些词可以用。

700
00:29:25.390 --> 00:29:25.830
I know.
我知道。

701
00:29:25.990 --> 00:29:27.010
We got nothing.
我们什么都没记住。

702
00:29:27.830 --> 00:29:28.910
We got lady.
我们只记住了“女士”。

703
00:29:29.350 --> 00:29:30.050
That's it.
就是这样。

704
00:29:30.150 --> 00:29:34.670
But you have to, like, if I'm familiar enough with someone to call them lady, I know their name.
但你得明白，如果我和某人熟到能叫她“女士”，我肯定知道她的名字。

705
00:29:34.990 --> 00:29:35.290
Right.
没错。

706
00:29:35.290 --> 00:29:39.050
I'm not going to call, you know, someone I barely interact with.
我可不会去叫那些我几乎没怎么打过交道的人。

707
00:29:39.190 --> 00:29:39.410
You're not going to be at the gas station.
你总不会在加油站那样吧。

708
00:29:39.470 --> 00:29:40.190
Hey, lady.
嘿，女士。

709
00:29:40.450 --> 00:29:40.610
Yeah.
是啊。

710
00:29:40.730 --> 00:29:41.530
Good morning, lady.
早上好，女士。

711
00:29:41.970 --> 00:29:43.310
No, I don't think so.
不，我觉得不会。

712
00:29:44.730 --> 00:29:46.030
But isn't this everyone?
但这不是每个人都会遇到的吗？

713
00:29:46.030 --> 00:29:48.290
We all suffer from this, right, guys?
我们都有这个毛病，对吧，伙计们？

714
00:29:48.290 --> 00:29:50.970
I mean, everybody has this problem.
我是说，每个人都有这个问题。

715
00:29:51.230 --> 00:29:55.450
How many people out there hear a name once and they lock into it?
有多少人能听一次名字就牢牢记住的？

716
00:29:55.510 --> 00:29:57.130
The percentage must be small.
比例肯定很小。

717
00:29:57.390 --> 00:30:03.090
Can we just all agree that we're not going to be offended if someone has to ask us our name 70 times?
我们能不能达成共识，如果有人问了我们70次名字，我们也不会感到被冒犯？

718
00:30:03.310 --> 00:30:05.650
Can that just be like a collective stress?
能不能把它当作一种集体压力？

719
00:30:06.310 --> 00:30:07.270
A collective forgiveness.
一种集体宽恕。

720
00:30:07.330 --> 00:30:08.270
We release that.
我们放下它吧。

721
00:30:08.390 --> 00:30:10.530
There's so much to be stressed about.
有太多事情值得我们操心了。

722
00:30:10.690 --> 00:30:12.950
And we can be judgy about other stuff.
我们可以在其他事情上评头论足。

723
00:30:13.090 --> 00:30:16.130
I want to just drop the name forgetting thing.
我只想放弃纠结记不住名字这件事。

724
00:30:16.410 --> 00:30:17.610
Let's just drop it.
我们就把它放下吧。

725
00:30:18.290 --> 00:30:18.470
It's fine.
没关系的。

726
00:30:18.670 --> 00:30:20.190
I don't care if you forgot my name.
我不在乎你是不是忘了我的名字。

727
00:30:20.330 --> 00:30:20.810
It's fine.
没关系的。

728
00:30:21.150 --> 00:30:22.810
I don't know how we get this out there.
我不知道该怎么把这个想法推广出去。

729
00:30:22.890 --> 00:30:25.150
I feel like it needs to be on a ballot or something.
我觉得这得像投票表决一样才行。

730
00:30:25.170 --> 00:30:26.630
We want a collective forgiveness.
我们需要集体宽恕。

731
00:30:26.910 --> 00:30:28.430
Collective forgiveness on names.
对名字的集体宽恕。

732
00:30:28.590 --> 00:30:29.950
Some days I'm amazing at it.
有时候我记性好得惊人。

733
00:30:30.070 --> 00:30:31.190
Some days I crush it.
有时候我表现得棒极了。

734
00:30:31.310 --> 00:30:33.670
But then there's my Ryan and Brian days.
但也有我把瑞安和布莱恩搞混的日子。

735
00:30:34.010 --> 00:30:38.530
Well, Andy's going to begin his tour of Dunder Mifflin at reception.
安迪要从前台开始他的邓德·米福林公司参观之旅了。

736
00:30:38.890 --> 00:30:39.370
Erinville.
艾琳维尔。

737
00:30:39.790 --> 00:30:40.210
Yes.
是的。

738
00:30:40.810 --> 00:30:43.790
Should we have two secretaries?
我们应该有两个秘书吗？

739
00:30:44.030 --> 00:30:44.830
Two receptionists?
两个前台接待员？

740
00:30:45.590 --> 00:30:45.910
Hmm.
嗯。

741
00:30:46.350 --> 00:30:47.550
Andy doesn't think so.
安迪不这么认为。

742
00:30:47.550 --> 00:30:49.610
Maybe Susan would be good for sales.
也许苏珊适合做销售。

743
00:30:49.770 --> 00:30:54.350
Let's go talk to Jim where, you know, Andy's sure Jim's going to have my back.
我们去和吉姆谈谈，你知道的，安迪确信吉姆会支持我。

744
00:30:54.510 --> 00:30:56.130
He's going to make sales sound horrible.
他会把销售工作描述得极其糟糕。

745
00:30:56.730 --> 00:30:59.530
But then Dwight comes over and makes sales sound amazing.
但随后德怀特走过来，把销售工作描述得无比美妙。

746
00:31:00.030 --> 00:31:06.050
So much so that after her first sale, Susan and Dwight are going to go have a glass of red wine
以至于在完成第一笔销售后，苏珊和德怀特打算去喝杯红酒，

747
00:31:06.050 --> 00:31:09.230
and trade their lists of best animals, their rankings.
顺便交流一下他们各自的最佳动物排名。

748
00:31:09.690 --> 00:31:11.750
She's fitting in pretty well with Dwight.
她和德怀特相处得相当融洽。

749
00:31:11.750 --> 00:31:14.270
This really stresses out Andy.
这让安迪感到非常紧张。

750
00:31:14.430 --> 00:31:16.890
He's like, ugh, how am I going to do this?
他心想，哎呀，我该怎么做呢？

751
00:31:17.110 --> 00:31:23.830
And lady, I think we're about to learn something that might confirm what Michael knew all along.
女士，我想我们即将了解到一些事情，这或许能证实迈克尔一直以来的猜想。

752
00:31:24.510 --> 00:31:26.690
Proof of Phyllis's flatulence.
关于菲利斯放屁的证据。

753
00:31:27.350 --> 00:31:27.710
Yes.
没错。

754
00:31:27.950 --> 00:31:32.790
Andy has a talking head about why couldn't Phyllis have one of her room-clearing farts.
安迪有个采访镜头，讲的是为什么菲利斯就不能放个能把房间清空的屁。

755
00:31:32.790 --> 00:31:38.370
It's, this definitely made me wonder if she really tooted at her wedding after all.
这确实让我怀疑她婚礼上到底是不是真的放屁了。

756
00:31:38.590 --> 00:31:40.010
That's what I think.
我也是这么想的。

757
00:31:40.130 --> 00:31:40.490
Right?
对吧？

758
00:31:40.850 --> 00:31:41.290
Yes.
没错。

759
00:31:41.910 --> 00:31:44.930
Here's one other thing I want to say about this Andy talking head.
关于安迪的这个采访镜头，我还想说点别的。

760
00:31:45.210 --> 00:31:49.630
There were several candy bag alts for it that were so hilarious.
当时有好几个备选的“糖果袋”台词，都特别搞笑。

761
00:31:49.850 --> 00:31:52.070
There were two pages of candy bag alts.
足足有两页纸的备选台词。

762
00:31:52.470 --> 00:31:55.630
Three of them really made me laugh hard, and I want to share them.
其中三个真的让我笑得不行，我想分享一下。

763
00:31:55.750 --> 00:31:55.910
Okay?
好吗？

764
00:31:55.910 --> 00:31:56.130
Okay.
好的。

765
00:31:56.970 --> 00:31:57.290
Andy.
安迪。

766
00:31:57.690 --> 00:31:59.330
How am I supposed to pull this off?
我到底该怎么搞定这一切？

767
00:31:59.510 --> 00:32:01.250
Kevin wore deodorant today.
凯文今天用了除臭剂。

768
00:32:01.730 --> 00:32:02.670
Angela smiled.
安吉拉笑了。

769
00:32:02.970 --> 00:32:04.890
Meredith ate before she drank.
梅雷迪斯喝酒前先吃了东西。

770
00:32:05.270 --> 00:32:06.350
Gee, thanks, team.
天哪，谢了，各位。

771
00:32:06.510 --> 00:32:07.030
Way to go.
干得漂亮。

772
00:32:08.910 --> 00:32:09.930
Here's the other one.
这是另一个。

773
00:32:10.270 --> 00:32:12.010
How am I supposed to pull this off?
我到底该怎么搞定这一切？

774
00:32:12.430 --> 00:32:16.890
Creed talked to her without a single spit bubble forming in the corner of his mouth.
克里德跟她说话时，嘴角竟然没冒出一个唾沫泡泡。

775
00:32:17.210 --> 00:32:17.590
Really?
真的吗？

776
00:32:17.890 --> 00:32:19.670
That hasn't happened in a decade.
这可是十年没发生过的事了。

777
00:32:20.850 --> 00:32:21.710
Last one.
最后一个。

778
00:32:22.030 --> 00:32:25.130
This is one where, you know, sometimes they throw a crazy one in there.
这个嘛，你知道，有时候他们会塞进去一个特别疯狂的。

779
00:32:25.230 --> 00:32:25.490
Yeah.
是啊。

780
00:32:26.070 --> 00:32:27.990
How am I supposed to pull this off?
我到底该怎么搞定这一切？

781
00:32:28.210 --> 00:32:32.950
I'm doing my best to make these assholes look like assholes, but these assholes keep
我尽力想让这帮混蛋看起来像个混蛋，但这帮混蛋却

782
00:32:32.950 --> 00:32:34.990
acting like pretty good people to work with.
表现得像是挺好相处的同事。

783
00:32:35.350 --> 00:32:36.950
These are all amazing.
这些都太棒了。

784
00:32:38.090 --> 00:32:39.190
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

785
00:32:39.310 --> 00:32:39.630
I know.
我知道。

786
00:32:39.730 --> 00:32:41.130
It was a really good candy bag.
那真的是个很棒的“糖果袋”。

787
00:32:41.470 --> 00:32:43.370
Lady, thank you so much for sharing those.
女士，非常感谢你分享这些。

788
00:32:43.510 --> 00:32:48.070
I think it's also really great for people out there who are maybe wanting to be writers
我觉得对于那些可能想成为作家

789
00:32:48.070 --> 00:32:54.350
or artists or artists or whatever to see how, like, our writers, they didn't write one talking
或艺术家之类的人来说，看到我们的编剧如何工作真的很有意义，他们不会只写一个采访镜头

790
00:32:54.350 --> 00:32:56.350
head or one button for a scene.
或者只给一个场景写一个结尾梗。

791
00:32:56.510 --> 00:32:57.670
They wrote a bunch.
他们会写上一大堆。

792
00:32:57.810 --> 00:32:58.190
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

793
00:32:58.410 --> 00:32:58.750
You know?
你知道吗？

794
00:32:58.750 --> 00:33:03.470
It's like you try everything and you see what ends up working beSt.
就像是你尝试各种可能，然后看看最终哪个效果最好。

795
00:33:03.730 --> 00:33:05.450
But there's so many good ones.
但真的有太多好的选择了。

796
00:33:05.550 --> 00:33:07.250
Like, any one of those would have cracked me up.
随便拿出一个来都能把我逗乐。

797
00:33:07.390 --> 00:33:07.810
Same.
我也是。

798
00:33:08.190 --> 00:33:13.310
Well, now Dwight is going to unveil his amazingly fancy gym to Daryl.
好了，现在德怀特要向达里尔展示他那“极其豪华”的健身房了。

799
00:33:13.430 --> 00:33:18.010
And by amazingly fancy, it looks like something out of a scene in Saw 5.
至于所谓的“极其豪华”，看起来就像是《电锯惊魂5》里的场景。

800
00:33:18.590 --> 00:33:18.990
Yes.
没错。

801
00:33:19.570 --> 00:33:23.910
This gym, it reminded me of the Strongest Man competition.
这家健身房让我想起了“世界大力士”比赛。

802
00:33:24.450 --> 00:33:26.770
Do you watch the Strongest Man competition?
你看过“世界大力士”比赛吗？

803
00:33:27.170 --> 00:33:30.150
Well, is that the one where they have to throw a log in the air?
嗯，是那种要把圆木扔到空中的比赛吗？

804
00:33:30.410 --> 00:33:30.770
Yes.
是的。

805
00:33:31.050 --> 00:33:35.710
So Dwight's gym, it has, like, there's just, like, a stump with, like, an axe.
所以德怀特的健身房里，就只有个树墩子和一把斧头。

806
00:33:36.050 --> 00:33:39.610
And there's just, like, gravel buckets and phone book ripping.
还有几桶碎石，以及用来撕的电话簿。

807
00:33:40.110 --> 00:33:43.470
So the Strongest Man competition, it started in 1977.
“世界大力士”比赛始于1977年。

808
00:33:43.850 --> 00:33:47.910
I looked up a description of it, and this could be written by Dwight.
我查了一下它的介绍，感觉这简直就是德怀特写的。

809
00:33:48.010 --> 00:33:48.990
It's amazing.
太绝了。

810
00:33:49.130 --> 00:33:49.670
Let's hear it.
念来听听。

811
00:33:50.150 --> 00:33:53.830
The World's Strongest Man competition is about more than just force.
“世界大力士”比赛不仅仅关乎力量。

812
00:33:54.070 --> 00:33:58.410
It is about stamina, skill, tactics, training, and strategy.
它还关乎耐力、技巧、战术、训练和策略。

813
00:33:58.950 --> 00:34:03.030
Every event is designed to push the strong men to their absolute limits,
每一项赛事的设计都是为了将大力士们的潜能推向极限，

814
00:34:03.270 --> 00:34:07.910
challenging not only their physical strength, but their agility and mental toughness, too.
不仅挑战他们的体力，还挑战他们的敏捷度和心理韧性。

815
00:34:08.350 --> 00:34:09.570
Doesn't that seem like—
这听起来是不是——

816
00:34:09.570 --> 00:34:10.770
That sounds very Dwight.
这听起来非常德怀特。

817
00:34:10.810 --> 00:34:11.510
Very Dwight.
非常德怀特。

818
00:34:11.850 --> 00:34:17.230
But yeah, they, like, lift giant tree trunks and boulders, and then they have an event.
不过确实，他们会举起巨大的树干和巨石，然后还有个项目。

819
00:34:17.800 --> 00:34:18.930
This is the one that gets me.
这个项目最让我震惊。

820
00:34:19.230 --> 00:34:20.350
The vehicle pull.
拉载具比赛。

821
00:34:20.870 --> 00:34:25.190
Oh, do they put the thing around their waist and then have to walk pulling a car or something?
哦，他们是把带子系在腰上，然后拉着车之类的东西走吗？

822
00:34:25.370 --> 00:34:27.050
Yes, but they don't just pull cars.
是的，但他们不只是拉汽车。

823
00:34:27.210 --> 00:34:28.290
They pull all kinds of stuff.
他们什么都拉。

824
00:34:28.410 --> 00:34:29.710
One time they pulled planes.
有一次他们拉的是飞机。

825
00:34:29.890 --> 00:34:30.390
A plane.
飞机？

826
00:34:30.390 --> 00:34:33.970
Is it stripped down, or is it an actual full plane?
是拆解过的，还是完整的飞机？

827
00:34:34.350 --> 00:34:35.690
I am not exactly sure.
我不太确定。

828
00:34:36.190 --> 00:34:38.990
I mean, listen, stripped down or not, it's still a f***ing plane.
我是说，听着，不管拆没拆，那可是一架他妈的飞机啊。

829
00:34:39.050 --> 00:34:41.610
It's a giant, and they have the weight and everything.
那是个庞然大物，重量什么的都在那儿摆着呢。

830
00:34:41.850 --> 00:34:48.110
And then the way they do it is it's like they have to drag it 100 feet in the quickest time possible.
他们的比赛方式是，看谁能以最快速度把它拖行100英尺。

831
00:34:48.110 --> 00:34:52.210
So whoever drags it the fastest is the winner of that competition.
所以谁拖得最快，谁就是那个项目的冠军。

832
00:34:52.450 --> 00:34:59.590
But, like, each year it's a different vehicle, and it kind of matches either, like, a strong man's profession.
而且每年拉的载具都不一样，通常会和某位大力士的职业挂钩。

833
00:34:59.590 --> 00:35:02.950
Like, one time there was a guy who was a firefighter, so they all—
比如有一次有个选手是消防员，所以他们就——

834
00:35:02.950 --> 00:35:03.630
Fire truck.
消防车。

835
00:35:03.630 --> 00:35:04.850
They pulled fire trucks.
他们拉的是消防车。

836
00:35:04.990 --> 00:35:11.470
