00:40:14.050 --> 00:40:19.890
In the ads, Kim says she was able to ditch her personal trainer because of the shoes because
在广告里，金说她因为穿了这双鞋就能甩掉私人教练，因为

960
00:40:19.890 --> 00:40:24.030
the idea was that these shoes were all the workout you needed because they had that little
当时的概念是，这双鞋就是你所需要的全部锻炼，因为它们有那个小小的

961
00:40:24.030 --> 00:40:26.650
foam thing that you were talking about in the shoe.
你刚才提到的鞋底泡沫垫。

962
00:40:27.250 --> 00:40:33.210
There were lawsuits filed against Skechers for these misleading ads because they conducted
斯凯奇因为这些误导性广告被起诉了，因为他们对

963
00:40:33.210 --> 00:40:38.790
studies on the target market, and they found that most people were misled into thinking
目标市场进行了研究，发现大多数人被误导，以为

964
00:40:38.790 --> 00:40:43.210
that the shoes alone would make them healthier, and most of the people who bought the shoes
单靠这双鞋就能让他们更健康，而大多数买了鞋的人

965
00:40:43.210 --> 00:40:45.830
gained weight because they ditched the gym.
反而增重了，因为他们不去健身房了。

966
00:40:46.010 --> 00:40:47.370
I looked into this.
我查了一下。

967
00:40:47.650 --> 00:40:54.850
Skechers had to pay $40 million to settle this lawsuit of these shoes that Kelly is wearing.
斯凯奇不得不支付4000万美元来和解这起关于凯莉脚上那双鞋的诉讼。

968
00:40:55.050 --> 00:40:57.710
Yes, the FTC settlement.
没错，就是联邦贸易委员会的和解协议。

969
00:40:58.430 --> 00:40:58.770
Wow.
哇。

970
00:40:59.150 --> 00:41:00.930
That's an expensive pair of shoes.
那可真是双昂贵的鞋子。

971
00:41:01.230 --> 00:41:05.450
Thank you, Mary Grace, for that amazing bit of info.
谢谢你，玛丽·格蕾丝，提供了这么棒的信息。

972
00:41:05.450 --> 00:41:11.710
I have a little accounting shout-out because I loved, loved, loved whenever the writers
我还要特别提一下会计组，因为我超爱、超爱、超爱编剧们

973
00:41:11.710 --> 00:41:17.910
would write something for Angela, Oscar, and Kevin that was just full of assumed history,
为安吉拉、奥斯卡和凯文写的那些充满背景设定的戏份，

974
00:41:17.910 --> 00:41:20.130
even if it was just a throwaway line.
哪怕那只是一句随口带过的台词。

975
00:41:20.350 --> 00:41:23.250
Because, you know, Oscar says, like, I need more gym drama.
因为，你知道，奥斯卡说，我需要更多健身房的八卦。

976
00:41:23.370 --> 00:41:26.970
And he starts listing all the different dynamics at the gym where he works out.
然后他开始列举他在健身房锻炼时遇到的各种人际关系。

977
00:41:27.090 --> 00:41:29.910
And Angela goes, enough, Oscar, enough.
安吉拉就说，够了，奥斯卡，够了。

978
00:41:31.330 --> 00:41:35.930
And you just know that he comes into work, and he's like, you would not believe who's
你完全能想象他来上班时说，你绝对不敢相信今天是谁

979
00:41:35.930 --> 00:41:38.030
doing leg day today and taking up all the machines.
在练腿日占用了所有的器械。

980
00:41:38.130 --> 00:41:42.490
Like, you would just imagine his gripe over there, and Angela's just over it.
你完全能想象他在那儿抱怨，而安吉拉已经听腻了。

981
00:41:42.610 --> 00:41:44.930
I feel like this is a little bit of a callback, too.
我觉得这也有点像是一个呼应。

982
00:41:45.110 --> 00:41:50.370
Remember in the previous episode when Oscar knew who was the most fit person when they
还记得上一集里，当他们在找仓库员工时，

983
00:41:50.370 --> 00:41:51.970
were looking for warehouse people?
奥斯卡一眼就看出了谁最健壮吗？

984
00:41:51.970 --> 00:41:53.630
He talks a lot about his gym.
他经常提起他的健身房。

985
00:41:54.030 --> 00:41:54.150
Yeah.
是的。

986
00:41:54.710 --> 00:41:56.370
Susan has arrived in HR.
苏珊到了人力资源部。

987
00:41:56.390 --> 00:41:59.170
She's going to do her, I guess, her paperwork, right?
她要去办她的，我想是她的入职手续，对吧？

988
00:41:59.370 --> 00:42:00.570
Her startup paperwork.
她的入职文书工作。

989
00:42:01.290 --> 00:42:03.450
And Toby asks her for her passport.
托比向她要护照。

990
00:42:05.290 --> 00:42:08.810
She just, in one sentence, destroys him.
她只用一句话就让他无地自容了。

991
00:42:08.950 --> 00:42:09.310
I know.
我知道。

992
00:42:09.430 --> 00:42:10.350
She's like, well, no.
她说，呃，没有。

993
00:42:10.450 --> 00:42:12.390
I mean, who walks around with her passport?
我是说，谁会随身带着护照啊？

994
00:42:12.670 --> 00:42:16.310
And Toby's like, well, I do, you know, just in case there's an adventure.
托比说，嗯，我会啊，你知道，万一有什么冒险呢。

995
00:42:16.990 --> 00:42:19.430
And she goes, have you been on any adventures?
然后她说，你经历过什么冒险吗？

996
00:42:19.570 --> 00:42:20.250
He's like, no.
他说，没有。

997
00:42:20.810 --> 00:42:22.030
Here was my question.
我有个疑问。

998
00:42:22.690 --> 00:42:26.230
Does he keep his passport on him at all times for adventures?
他是为了冒险才随时带着护照吗？

999
00:42:26.590 --> 00:42:30.230
Or in case he has to flee because he is the Scranton Strangler?
还是为了万一需要逃跑，因为他就是斯克兰顿勒杀手？

1000
00:42:30.370 --> 00:42:31.310
Well, there you go.
好吧，这下真相大白了。

1001
00:42:31.450 --> 00:42:32.610
Evidence of strangling?
有勒死的痕迹吗？

1002
00:42:32.770 --> 00:42:33.630
Maybe so.
或许吧。

1003
00:42:34.010 --> 00:42:37.730
We had a fan catch in this scene that so delighted me.
这一幕里有个粉丝发现的细节，让我觉得特别有意思。

1004
00:42:38.010 --> 00:42:42.270
I didn't notice it when I watched the episode, but when I went back to check after I read
我第一次看这集的时候没注意到，但读到这个粉丝提问后，

1005
00:42:42.270 --> 00:42:44.530
this fan question, I laughed out loud.
我回去核实了一下，结果笑出声来。

1006
00:42:45.610 --> 00:42:46.410
Allison H.
来自挪威的

1007
00:42:46.590 --> 00:42:47.390
from Norway said,
Allison H. 问道：

1008
00:42:47.390 --> 00:42:52.170
Why is Toby's chair so low and his desk so high?
为什么托比的椅子那么低，桌子却那么高？

1009
00:42:52.950 --> 00:42:54.430
Oh, my gosh, Angela.
天哪，安吉拉。

1010
00:42:54.770 --> 00:42:55.870
His desk?
他的桌子？

1011
00:42:56.070 --> 00:42:58.070
It's in his armpit.
都快顶到他咯吱窝了。

1012
00:42:58.670 --> 00:43:00.090
I took pictures.
我拍了照片。

1013
00:43:00.350 --> 00:43:00.910
Let me see.
让我看看。

1014
00:43:00.990 --> 00:43:01.870
I'm putting on my glasses.
我戴上眼镜看看。

1015
00:43:02.730 --> 00:43:03.850
Swipe to look.
往后滑看下一张。

1016
00:43:03.970 --> 00:43:05.110
That is a far away.
那张拍得太远了。

1017
00:43:05.230 --> 00:43:06.390
And then I did a close-up.
然后我拍了一张特写。

1018
00:43:07.190 --> 00:43:07.750
What?
什么？

1019
00:43:07.990 --> 00:43:09.310
Who sits like that?
谁会那样坐着？

1020
00:43:09.510 --> 00:43:10.390
You know what?
你知道吗？

1021
00:43:10.490 --> 00:43:14.190
I bet he got the crap chair that we kept passing around.
我敢打赌他坐的是我们一直推来推去的那把破椅子。

1022
00:43:14.190 --> 00:43:14.570
Remember?
还记得吗？

1023
00:43:14.830 --> 00:43:16.970
Sometimes you would come on set and you'd be like,
有时候你来到片场会说：

1024
00:43:17.050 --> 00:43:19.010
Who the heck put the crap chair?
到底是谁把这把破椅子放这儿的？

1025
00:43:19.110 --> 00:43:20.130
The one that wouldn't go up and down.
就是那把没法升降的椅子。

1026
00:43:20.130 --> 00:43:21.230
It wouldn't go up and down.
它根本没法升降。

1027
00:43:21.230 --> 00:43:24.350
And we kept moving it back to the annex or moving it somewhere else.
我们一直把它挪到附楼或者其他什么地方。

1028
00:43:24.530 --> 00:43:26.030
But why was this allowed?
但为什么会允许这种情况存在呢？

1029
00:43:26.250 --> 00:43:29.210
Like, you'd think, like, when it was time to shoot, they would be like,
你会觉得，拍摄的时候，他们应该会说：

1030
00:43:29.250 --> 00:43:30.530
We gotta get this guy.
我们得给这哥们儿换把椅子。

1031
00:43:30.650 --> 00:43:30.950
Yeah.
是啊。

1032
00:43:31.690 --> 00:43:32.090
Yeah.
没错。

1033
00:43:32.310 --> 00:43:33.090
A real chair.
一把真正的椅子。

1034
00:43:33.450 --> 00:43:33.770
That is so funny.
太搞笑了。

1035
00:43:34.130 --> 00:43:35.490
It was delightful.
这真的很有趣。

1036
00:43:35.970 --> 00:43:37.010
Great catch, Allison.
发现得好，Allison。

1037
00:43:38.050 --> 00:43:40.470
Andy has a new strategy for getting rid of Susan,
安迪有个打发苏珊的新策略，

1038
00:43:40.470 --> 00:43:44.610
which is that he's gonna tell everyone in the bullpen to make it a miserable place to work,
他打算告诉办公区的所有人，要把这里变成一个让人待不下去的地方，

1039
00:43:44.790 --> 00:43:47.090
so miserable that she wants to leave by lunch.
惨到让她午饭前就想走人。

1040
00:43:48.150 --> 00:43:49.770
And, you know, Jim is gonna say,
然后，吉姆会说：

1041
00:43:49.930 --> 00:43:52.890
I don't think we should try to make this place seem unpleasant.
我觉得我们没必要故意让这里显得不愉快。

1042
00:43:52.890 --> 00:43:56.290
I think we should just let this place crush her spirit by itself.
我觉得我们应该让这个地方自己去摧毁她的精神。

1043
00:43:56.330 --> 00:43:57.950
I mean, it knows what it's doing.
我是说，它自己知道该怎么做。

1044
00:43:58.170 --> 00:43:59.270
That made me laugh.
那段把我逗笑了。

1045
00:43:59.490 --> 00:44:01.710
I also loved when Erin goes,
我也很喜欢艾琳说的那句：

1046
00:44:01.850 --> 00:44:03.610
I know exactly what stapler to give her.
我知道该给她哪个订书机。

1047
00:44:03.710 --> 00:44:03.850
Yes.
没错。

1048
00:44:04.550 --> 00:44:06.330
And then we had the tiny one.
然后我们拿出了那个超小的订书机。

1049
00:44:06.690 --> 00:44:07.550
It's like so ridiculous.
简直太荒谬了。

1050
00:44:07.850 --> 00:44:09.170
That joke tastes so well.
那个梗真是百看不厌。

1051
00:44:09.170 --> 00:44:12.690
No way, Ellie, like, as Erin placed it on the table, too.
没门，艾莉，就像艾琳把它放在桌子上时那样。

1052
00:44:12.730 --> 00:44:12.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1053
00:44:13.390 --> 00:44:14.990
Look what I've had to deal with.
看看我得应付些什么。

1054
00:44:15.750 --> 00:44:18.410
Well, there was an alt-talking head for Jim,
嗯，吉姆有个备用的访谈片段，

1055
00:44:18.410 --> 00:44:23.210
and we find out a little something about Stanley that I want you all to hear.
我们从中发现了一些关于斯坦利的趣事，我想让你们都听听。

1056
00:44:23.430 --> 00:44:23.730
Okay.
好的。

1057
00:44:24.370 --> 00:44:26.390
This whole thing is making me very uncomfortable.
这一切让我感到非常不自在。

1058
00:44:27.050 --> 00:44:28.950
I'm not getting in between the boss and his wife,
我可不想夹在老板和他妻子中间，

1059
00:44:29.030 --> 00:44:30.310
so just ask me about something else.
所以问我点别的吧。

1060
00:44:31.370 --> 00:44:34.290
You know, Stanley's tie is really the story of the day.
你知道，斯坦利的领带才是今天的主角。

1061
00:44:36.540 --> 00:44:37.680
It's my birthday.
今天是我的生日。

1062
00:44:38.920 --> 00:44:42.410
Oh, it's been Stanley's birthday?
噢，今天是斯坦利的生日吗？

1063
00:44:42.710 --> 00:44:42.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1064
00:44:44.880 --> 00:44:45.760
Where is his party?
他的派对在哪儿？

1065
00:44:46.040 --> 00:44:48.240
What has happened to the party planning committee?
派对策划委员会到底怎么了？

1066
00:44:49.000 --> 00:44:51.840
And the best thing is when he says,
最棒的是当他说，

1067
00:44:52.100 --> 00:44:53.000
it is my birthday,
今天是我的生日时，

1068
00:44:53.000 --> 00:44:56.480
they do a full pan shot of his tie,
镜头会完整地扫过他的领带，

1069
00:44:56.720 --> 00:44:59.520
and his tie is a long blue fish,
那条领带是一条长长的蓝色鱼，

1070
00:44:59.540 --> 00:45:02.320
and the face of it is the end of the tie.
鱼脸就在领带的末端。

1071
00:45:02.460 --> 00:45:02.720
Okay.
好的。

1072
00:45:03.160 --> 00:45:04.820
It is a hilarious tie.
那条领带太搞笑了。

1073
00:45:05.200 --> 00:45:07.980
He's clearly worn special for his birthday.
他显然是为了生日特意戴的。

1074
00:45:08.680 --> 00:45:11.940
In the whole episode, I rewatched it looking for this tie.
整集节目里，我重看了一遍就是为了找这条领带。

1075
00:45:12.100 --> 00:45:13.540
You only see the top of it.
你只能看到它的顶部。

1076
00:45:13.760 --> 00:45:14.340
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

1077
00:45:14.340 --> 00:45:15.660
You just see the blue top.
你只能看到蓝色的顶部。

1078
00:45:15.740 --> 00:45:18.000
But if it had ever shown him standing,
但如果镜头拍到他站着的话，

1079
00:45:18.000 --> 00:45:20.000
you would have seen the fish face.
你就能看到鱼脸了。

1080
00:45:20.780 --> 00:45:22.600
But it's Stanley's birthday.
但今天是斯坦利的生日。

1081
00:45:23.180 --> 00:45:24.800
Well, Pam is gone.
好吧，帕姆不在。

1082
00:45:25.260 --> 00:45:27.340
Maybe she was in charge of this.
也许她负责这件事。

1083
00:45:27.460 --> 00:45:28.100
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

1084
00:45:28.100 --> 00:45:29.560
What is Kathy for?
凯西是干什么用的？

1085
00:45:29.920 --> 00:45:30.620
I don't know.
我不知道。

1086
00:45:30.760 --> 00:45:31.380
Pam is gone.
帕姆不在。

1087
00:45:31.500 --> 00:45:32.240
Angela's retired.
安吉拉退休了。

1088
00:45:32.400 --> 00:45:34.600
And Kathy is not doing her job.
而凯西没在做她的工作。

1089
00:45:34.920 --> 00:45:37.040
No, not if Pam was in charge of birthday.
不，如果帕姆负责生日的话，那就不一样了。

1090
00:45:37.040 --> 00:45:37.660
She's not.
她没负责。

1091
00:45:38.000 --> 00:45:40.680
This is actually a good segue for me into the next scene.
这正好可以让我顺势过渡到下一个场景。

1092
00:45:40.840 --> 00:45:42.180
We're in the break room,
我们在休息室里，

1093
00:45:42.260 --> 00:45:44.100
and Oscar's passing around his phone
奥斯卡正在传阅他的手机，

1094
00:45:44.100 --> 00:45:46.600
to kind of show everyone his, like, new puppy
给每个人看他的，呃，新小狗，

1095
00:45:46.600 --> 00:45:49.180
who has crawled into a Williams-Sonoma ladle.
它爬进了一个威廉姆斯-索诺玛的汤勺里。

1096
00:45:49.460 --> 00:45:49.780
Gerald.
杰拉德。

1097
00:45:50.220 --> 00:45:50.700
Yes.
是的。

1098
00:45:50.700 --> 00:45:53.100
And they're not letting Susan see the picture.
而且他们不让苏珊看照片。

1099
00:45:53.380 --> 00:45:55.200
They're kind of freezing her out of the conversation.
他们有点把她排挤在谈话之外了。

1100
00:45:56.000 --> 00:45:58.940
We got a fan question from a lot of people.
我们收到了很多粉丝提出的同一个问题。

1101
00:45:59.180 --> 00:45:59.820
Gina S.
吉娜·S.

1102
00:46:00.060 --> 00:46:01.940
in Iowa, Meredith in Sacramento,
来自爱荷华州的，萨克拉门托的梅雷迪思，

1103
00:46:02.360 --> 00:46:03.760
Lauren from Peoria, Illinois,
来自伊利诺伊州皮奥里亚的劳伦，

1104
00:46:04.240 --> 00:46:05.360
who all said,
他们都说，

1105
00:46:05.460 --> 00:46:08.180
Jenna had to leave the show temporarily for maternity leave,
珍娜因为产假暂时离开了剧组，

1106
00:46:08.240 --> 00:46:09.380
but it has always bothered me
但我一直很困扰，

1107
00:46:09.380 --> 00:46:11.340
that Pam disappears with no fanfare.
帕姆的离开竟然毫无声息。

1108
00:46:11.560 --> 00:46:13.960
It seems like Jim would have been more excited
吉姆理应表现得更兴奋才对，

1109
00:46:13.960 --> 00:46:16.000
to share the birth of their second child
去分享他们第二个孩子的出生，

1110
00:46:16.000 --> 00:46:18.460
or the story of the delivery
或是讲述分娩的过程，

1111
00:46:18.460 --> 00:46:20.840
or maybe how mom and baby are doing.
又或者是说说母子平安的情况。

1112
00:46:21.020 --> 00:46:21.480
Something.
总得有点什么。

1113
00:46:21.660 --> 00:46:22.460
There's nothing.
结果什么都没有。

1114
00:46:22.880 --> 00:46:24.500
Was there a writing decision
这是编剧组的决定吗？

1115
00:46:24.500 --> 00:46:26.740
to not focus on this part of their lives?
不去关注他们生活中的这一部分？

1116
00:46:26.740 --> 00:46:28.520
I really would have loved to see more of Jim
我真的很想看到吉姆在这一集中，

1117
00:46:28.520 --> 00:46:31.420
acknowledging the addition to his family in this episode.
更多地表达他家庭新成员的到来。

1118
00:46:31.700 --> 00:46:32.680
Well, first of all,
嗯，首先，

1119
00:46:32.860 --> 00:46:35.080
Steve Burgess reminded me that my son was born
史蒂夫·伯吉斯提醒我，我的儿子

1120
00:46:35.080 --> 00:46:37.840
the Saturday before we started filming this episode.
是在我们开拍这一集的前一个周六出生的。

